# Camera Pipeline Contract Audit

## Purpose

Find the first failed or unknown edge from electrical bring-up to each effective frame consumer. Keep control, pixel, memory, and consumer paths separate: evidence from one never proves another.

## Required path

Audit every applicable layer in order:

`power/reset/clock → I2C control → CSI/MIPI → media/V4L2 → ISP → buffer/DMA → encoder/algorithm/consumer`

Include rails/sequencing/pinmux, sensor/EEPROM/SerDes identity, lanes/VC/data-type, media pads/links/sub-devices, negotiated mode, ISP ports, and actual consumers. Mark absent layers `not_applicable`.

Route unresolved loaded-artifact identity to `embedded-runtime-provenance`; route matched contracts with rate/latency/memory/thermal/soak failures to `embedded-performance-stability`.

## Procedure

### 1. Freeze scope

Record device/camera identity, requested mode, runtime artifacts, consumers, reproduction/window, and lifecycle: cold boot/restart/suspend-resume/repeated stream.

### 2. Enumerate nodes

List ordered nodes through every consumer. A device node, probe, link, dequeue, preview, or ISP log proves only that observation point.

### 3. Prove edge contracts

Compare expected versus observed per source→target edge:

- format: bus-code/pixel-format/bit-depth/color, dimensions/crop/scale, planes/stride/offsets/size;
- timing: FPS/sequence, timestamp point/domain/unit/monotonicity/offset/wrap/synchronization;
- transport/state: lanes/VC/data-type/bandwidth, media-link/queue/IPC, enable/error/recovery/warm-restore.

Never derive layout from width × height or compare clock domains without explicit conversion.

### 4. Trace `buffer_ownership`

Trace allocator/exporter/importer, owner transition, frame key, lifetime/refcount, map/unmap, DMA direction, cache maintenance, fences, queue/reuse/release, capacity/occupancy/wait/drop/starvation/backpressure. Correlate identity across transfers; delivery does not prove consumption.

### 5. Localize safely

Name last proven node, first failed/unknown edge, alternatives, and smallest probe. Default read-only. Power/reset/register, topology/format, bind/unbind, restart, or fault injection requires explicit authorization and rollback.

## Required output contract

### `pipeline_scope`

Device/camera, scenario/window, requested/observed mode, path/consumers, provenance, safety.

### `node_matrix`

| Order | Layer/node | Input | Output/state | Runtime identity | Evidence | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

Status: `proven`, `failed`, `unknown`, `not_applicable`.

### `edge_contract_matrix`

| Source→target | Interface | Format/layout/stride | Timing/timestamp domain | Transport/state | Expected/observed | Evidence | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

Split rows hiding independent control, pixel, or consumer contracts.

### `buffer_ownership`

| Frame/buffer key | Allocator/exporter→importer/owner | Transition/lifetime | DMA/cache/fence | Queue/backpressure/drop | Evidence | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

### `breakpoints`

Last proven node, first failed/unknown edge, negative evidence, alternatives, smallest read-only probe, authorized mutation/rollback.

### `verdict`

Per scenario/consumer: `supported`, `candidate`, `refuted`, or `unresolved`; include highest boundary, allowed/prohibited claims, missing evidence, owner. Aggregate preserves the weakest required path.

## Anti-patterns

- Treating `/dev/video*`, one dequeued frame, or ISP output as end-to-end proof.
- Blaming sensor/ISP before checking format, planes, stride, size, and consumer input.
- Mixing sensor counters, hardware, monotonic, and realtime clocks.
- Ignoring ownership, cache coherency, fences, saturation, backpressure, or drops.
- Mutating power, registers, topology, binding, or stream state merely to gather evidence.
